== exit code: 1
== stdout
List resources from a Dynatrace Managed environment.

Supported resources:
  environments          Configured Managed environments and cluster info
  problems (prob)       Active and resolved problems
  entities (ent)        Monitored entities (requires --selector)
  entity-types (et)     All available entity types
  events (ev)           Events within a time range
  metrics (met)         Available metric descriptors
  slos                  Service Level Objectives
  security-problems (sp) Security vulnerabilities

Use 'dtmgd get <resource> --help' for resource-specific options.

Usage:
  dtmgd get [flags]
  dtmgd get [command]

Available Commands:
  entities          Discover entities using an entity selector
  entity-types      List all available entity types
  environments      List configured Dynatrace Managed environments
  events            List events from the Dynatrace Managed environment
  metrics           List available metric descriptors
  problems          List problems from the Dynatrace Managed environment
  security-problems List security vulnerabilities
  slos              List Service Level Objectives

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for get

Global Flags:
  -A, --agent                     force agent envelope output mode
      --columns string            comma-separated list of columns to show in table output
      --concurrency int           maximum environments queried at once with --env (default 10)
      --config string             config file (default: ~/.config/dtmgd/config)
  -c, --context string            context to use (overrides current-context)
  -e, --env string                environment(s): context name, "prod;staging", or ALL_ENVIRONMENTS
      --max-pages int             maximum number of pages to fetch (0 = all pages)
      --no-agent                  disable auto-detected agent mode
  -o, --output string             output format: table|json|yaml|wide (default: table)
  -v, --verbose count             verbosity level (-v for summary, -vv for full request/response)
  -w, --watch                     re-run the command periodically
      --watch-interval duration   interval between watch refreshes (e.g. 5s, 30s, 1m) (default 5s)

Use "dtmgd get [command] --help" for more information about a command.
